This game is what I expected from Age of Wonders 3 and Civilization5, but never got.
It's a certain kind of people who play these games, most of them have infinite patience to get through "development" phase of the game to the point where actual fun begins. Never concidered myself one of them, still here I am: planning next research, redistributing workers each turn, building cities and moving armies (which takes a whole lot of a time, especially in winter — brace yourself). Yet, unlike AoW or CiV this doesn't get me wondering "what the hell am I wasting time on?".
Pros:
• Awesome art and atmosferic soundtrack;
• Each race's abilities greatelly impact the gameplay and strategy;
• Somehow not boring even on supersize map;
• Lot's of other great gamemechanics and things to do.
• Heroes actually CAN do a lot of good in the city as governors, without being turned into wondering slaughterhouse in order to get EXP and loot.
• Heroic traits actually DO impact the strategy of city development.
Cons:
• Few races;
• Cann't incenerate enemies with fireball to the face :(
• Few units;
• Probably, there are more, but 20+ hours into the game and haven't encountered em yet.
Hope, this was helpful.
